{"data":{"updated_timestamp":"12/11/2026 01:20:50","profile":{"player_id":"63717","last_updated":"12/11/2026 01:20","fullname":"Senuran Muthusamy","short_display_name":"S Muthusamy","name":"Senuran Muthusamy","gender":"M","dob":"22/02/1994","date_of_death":null,"place_birth":"South Africa","nationality_id":"7","nationality":"South Africa","nationality_short_code":"SA","nick_name":"Sen","player_skill":{"id":"3","text":"All Rounder","role":"All Rounder"},"batting_style":{"id":"2","text":"Left Handed"},"bowling_style":{"id":"15","text":"Slow left-arm orthodox"},"writeup":"<p>Senuran Muthusamy is a left-handed batsman who can also bowl some left-arm orthodox spells. Hailing from Durban, the southpaw made his First-class debut for KwaZulu-Natal in 2013. After his debut season, he shifted to the Dolphins team for the following year. The 2016-17 Sunfoil series was the turning point of his life after he smashed his career-best knock of 181 against the Knights. In the same series, Senuran bagged 27 scalps and ended the series on a high note. The stylish left-handed batsman has been one of the standout performers for the Dolphins in red-ball cricket for the last few seasons. Being a multi-dimensional player and providing enough balance to his side, Muthusamy was named in South Africa's Test squad for their series against India.</p>","relation":null,"social_details":{"social_platform":[{"social_platform_id":"1","social_platform_name":"facebook","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"2","social_platform_name":"twitter","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"3","social_platform_name":"instagram","social_platform_url":"https://www.instagram.com/senseii_67/"},{"social_platform_id":"4","social_platform_name":"youtube","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"5","social_platform_name":"pinterest","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"6","social_platform_name":"linkedin","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"7","social_platform_name":